\mt1 The Book of Psalms  
\c 51  
\d To the chief \w Musician\w*, A \w Psalm\w* of \w David\w*, when \w Nathan\w* the \w prophet\w* \w came\w* unto him, after he had gone \w in\w* to \w Bath-sheba\w*.  
\q1
\v 1 Have \w mercy\w* upon me, O \w God\w*, according to thy \w lovingkindness\w*: according unto the \w multitude\w* of thy tender \w mercies\w* blot \w out\w* my \w transgressions\w*.   
\q1
\v 2 \w Wash\w* me \w throughly\w* from mine \w iniquity\w*, and \w cleanse\w* me from my \w sin\w*.   
\q1
\v 3 For I \w acknowledge\w* my \w transgressions\w*: and my \w sin\w* \add is\add* \w ever\w* before me.   
\q1
\v 4 Against thee, thee only, have I \w sinned\w*, and \w done\w* \add this\add* \w evil\w* in thy \w sight\w*: that thou mightest be \w justified\w* when thou \w speakest\w*, \add and\add* be \w clear\w* when thou \w judgest\w*.   
\q1
\v 5 Behold, I was \w shapen\w* in \w iniquity\w*; and in \w sin\w* did my \w mother\w* \w conceive\w* me.\f + \fr 51.5 \ft conceive…: Heb. warm me\f*   
\q1
\v 6 Behold, thou \w desirest\w* \w truth\w* in the inward \w parts\w*: and in the \w hidden\w* \add part\add* thou shalt make me to \w know\w* \w wisdom\w*.   
\b  
\q1
\v 7 \w Purge\w* me with \w hyssop\w*, and I shall be \w clean\w*: \w wash\w* me, and I shall be \w whiter\w* than \w snow\w*.   
\q1
\v 8 Make me to \w hear\w* \w joy\w* and \w gladness\w*; \add that\add* the \w bones\w* \add which\add* thou hast \w broken\w* may \w rejoice\w*.   
\q1
\v 9 \w Hide\w* thy \w face\w* from my \w sins\w*, and blot \w out\w* all mine \w iniquities\w*.   
\q1
\v 10 \w Create\w* in me a \w clean\w* \w heart\w*, O \w God\w*; and \w renew\w* a \w right\w* \w spirit\w* \w within\w* me.\f + \fr 51.10 \ft right: or, constant\f*   
\q1
\v 11 Cast me not \w away\w* from thy \w presence\w*; and \w take\w* not thy \w holy\w* \w spirit\w* from me.   
\q1
\v 12 \w Restore\w* unto me the \w joy\w* of thy \w salvation\w*; and \w uphold\w* me \add with thy\add* \w free\w* \w spirit\w*.   
\q1
\v 13 \add Then\add* will I \w teach\w* \w transgressors\w* thy \w ways\w*; and \w sinners\w* shall be \w converted\w* unto thee.   
\b  
\q1
\v 14 \w Deliver\w* me from \w bloodguiltiness\w*, O \w God\w*, thou \w God\w* of my \w salvation\w*: \add and\add* my \w tongue\w* shall sing \w aloud\w* of thy \w righteousness\w*.\f + \fr 51.14 \ft bloodguiltiness: Heb. bloods\f*   
\q1
\v 15 O \w Lord\w*, \w open\w* thou my \w lips\w*; and my \w mouth\w* shall shew \w forth\w* thy \w praise\w*.   
\q1
\v 16 For thou \w desirest\w* not \w sacrifice\w*; else would I \w give\w* \add it:\add* thou \w delightest\w* not in burnt \w offering\w*.\f + \fr 51.16 \ft else…: or, that I should\f*   
\q1
\v 17 The \w sacrifices\w* of \w God\w* \add are\add* a \w broken\w* \w spirit\w*: a \w broken\w* and a \w contrite\w* \w heart\w*, O \w God\w*, thou wilt not \w despise\w*.   
\q1
\v 18 Do \w good\w* in thy good \w pleasure\w* unto \w Zion\w*: \w build\w* thou the \w walls\w* of \w Jerusalem\w*.   
\q1
\v 19 Then shalt thou be \w pleased\w* with the \w sacrifices\w* of \w righteousness\w*, with burnt \w offering\w* and \w whole\w* burnt \w offering\w*: then shall they \w offer\w* \w bullocks\w* upon thine \w altar\w*.
